expression equals $0$ at the points $x=-18$ and $x=2.$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}-2x\\le 9-6x$ for all \n\n$$\nx\\in [-18,2].\n$$" 13194139534094 true] [17592186277453 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277454 13194139534094 true] [17592186277453 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534094 true] [17592186277453 1041 "field-1" 13194139534094 true] [17592186277453 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277454 13194139534094 true] [17592186277453 1110 #uuid "291b5803-443c-5a1e-b7f3-1950fca5da99" 13194139534094 true] [17592186277454 1034 "-18" 13194139534094 true] [17592186277454 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534094 true] [17592186277454 1111 #uuid "8f498aa5-610b-532b-b4d2-cad59c2b1690" 13194139534094 true] [17592186277455 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277456 13194139534094 true] [17592186277455 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534094 true] [17592186277455 1041 "field-2" 13194139534094 true] [17592186277455 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277456 13194139534094 true] [17592186277455 1110 #uuid "df2024ec-266b-5fcf-8530-2ca324e3c007" 13194139534094 true] [17592186277456 1034 "2" 13194139534094 true] [17592186277456 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534094 true] [17592186277456 1111 #uuid "637db1ce-f2b8-5947-9d53-ea95c72af0d8" 13194139534094 true] [17592186277457 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277458 13194139534094 true] [17592186277457 1089 "q-70962" 13194139534094 true] [17592186277457 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534094 true] [17592186277457 1100 "For which values of $x$ is $2{x}^{2}-8x>0?$" 13194139534094 true] [17592186277457 1113 #uuid "af09d3a8-1383-5f69-bd64-b908058734c8" 13194139534094 true] [17592186277457 1145 "First, let's factor the left-hand side of the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-8x & >0 \\\\ 2x(x-4) & >0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the roots of the corresponding equation $2x(x-4)=0.$ The roots are $x=0$ and $x=4,$ and they split the number line into the $3$ intervals $(-\\infty ,0),$ $(0,4),$ and $(4,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, we construct a sign table with the list of the intervals on the top and the list of factors on the left. Filling in the sign table using the usual method, we get the following result:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,0)$ | $(0,4)$ | $(4,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x-4$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $2x(x-4)$ | $(-)\\cdot (-)=+$ | $(+)\\cdot (-)=-$ | $(+)\\cdot (+)=+$ |\n\nFinally, to solve the quadratic inequality $x(x-4)>0,$ we look at the bottom row to find out where the expression $2x(x-4)$ is positive.\n\nWe see that the expression is positive on the intervals $(-\\infty ,0)$ and $(4,\\infty ).$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that $2{x}^{2}-8x>0$ for all $x\\in (-\\infty ,0)\\cup (4,\\infty ).$" 13194139534094 true] [17592186277458 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277459 13194139534094 true] [17592186277458 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277460 13194139534094 true] [17592186277458 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277461 13194139534094 true] [17592186277458 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277462 13194139534094 true] [17592186277458 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277463 13194139534094 true] [17592186277458 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534094 true] [17592186277458 1041 "selection" 13194139534094 true] [17592186277458 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277463 13194139534094 true] [17592186277458 1110 #uuid "31779b32-2d92-597a-ac6a-c9d5cac4133c" 13194139534094 true] [17592186277459 1034 "x\\in (-\\infty ,-4)\\cup (0,\\infty )" 13194139534094 true] [17592186277459 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534094 true] [17592186277459 1111 #uuid "b08474a3-4bba-58d8-bb25-5b1292700cc5" 13194139534094 true] [17592186277460 1034 "x\\in (-4,0)" 13194139534094 true] [17592186277460 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534094 true] [17592186277460 1111 #uuid "b7f3bc96-6016-514a-a5a1-2e233ea530bf" 13194139534094 true] [17592186277461 1034 "x\\in (0,\\infty )" 13194139534094 true] [17592186277461 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534094 true] [17592186277461 1111 #uuid "417fd51e-d6bb-52e7-ae38-8de69fa1e20d" 13194139534094 true] [1759218627